course: dictionary
lesson: 11933
title: Calling things off
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cancellation is the act of calling off something that was planned. The verb is cancel, and the noun is cancellation. «There was a cancellation of the 9 o'clock train because of the snow.» The snow is the clue: the train was called off, so it did not run.
explain: The word can also mean a free space that appears when someone else cancels. «Mum rang the dentist and got a cancellation, so I could go in today.» Someone cancelled their appointment, so a place opened up. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Does "called off" or "free place" make the sentence make sense?
explain: In maths, cancellation is a different job. You remove a number that is shared by the top and bottom of a fraction to make it simpler. In 2/4, the 2 is on the top and the bottom, so you cancel it and get 1/2.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Cancellation is a noun, and its verb is cancel.
fact: «Cancellation» means the act of calling off something that was planned.
fact: A «cancellation fee» is money you pay for calling off a booking too late.
fact: In maths, cancelling removes a shared factor from the top and bottom of a fraction: 2/4 becomes 1/2.
exercise: «The concert had a cancellation because of the storm.» What does cancellation mean here? | The concert was longer than usual | The singers were given new costumes | The crowd cheered very loudly | *The concert was called off
exercise: Mum rang the hairdresser to get a cancellation for today. What is a cancellation here? | A brand new haircut | A very long wait for a seat | A phone call to a friend | *A free appointment, because someone else called theirs off
exercise: In maths, cancelling the shared 2 in 2/4 leaves which fraction? | 2/3 | 1/4 | 4/2 | *1/2
test: «The bus company announced a cancellation of the 9 o'clock bus.» What does cancellation mean? | The bus will run early | *The bus will not run | The bus is full of children | The bus is painted bright red
test: «Sam waited a week for a cancellation so he could have his swimming lesson.» What is a cancellation here? | A lesson that lasts a whole week | A new swimming pool | A special swimming costume | *A free place, because someone else cancelled
exam: What is a cancellation fee? | *Money you pay for calling off a booking too late | A free ticket to the cinema | A fee for catching a train on time | Money you win for coming first in a race
